From: j7 speed
Subject: j7 g3d: stop paying for the whole-AS verify, and name whoever clears a live mapping

The 2026-11-10 boot log with 0330 shows the pool is not the whole story: the pool is 4096 tables and
maps succeed, yet submits still fault ("fault at 3010400 in bo 5 ... translation level 2 execute",
"walk ... l2=... l3=0 leaf=0") and j7m_repair rewrites the same BO's leaves again and again
("fault repair: bo=44 va=39c1000 fixed=95"), while the table count climbs 705 -> 1863 -> 2546 ->
2914 of 4096.  A whole 2 MiB window entry is being cleared under a BO that is still live.

Three changes:

- audit: clear-path callers (j7m_unmap_page, j7m_release_l3) now check whether a live BO still owns
  the range they are about to clear and print one line naming it.  A BO being torn down is exempt.

- verify: 0328 walked every page of every BO on every submit (checked=17520 at 4 fps).  The tables
  only change when this driver writes or clears a mapping, so give the driver a map generation and
  re-walk only when it moved, plus once every 32nd submit as a safety net.

- pool: 16 MiB (4096 tables) was still exhausted in the fault-repair churn; ask for 64 MiB and say
  once when the pool is actually full, so exhaustion stops being a silent 5 s timeout.

